              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-364",
              ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^2 \\,\\textrm d x.$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "We apply the power rule with $n=2$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int x^2 \\,\\textrm d x = \\dfrac{x^{2+1}}{2+1} + C = \\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\ &= {x}^{2}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186064168,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186064039,
              ":question/id": "818f4fbe-e251-57bd-90ae-b6517c6f2f89",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-367",
              ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of  $\\sqrt x.$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "We start by writing the square root as a rational power, $\\sqrt x= x^{1/2}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{1/2+1}}{(\\frac{1}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3/2}}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{1/2}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "85af4ca3-5e66-522a-9e5a-6efb1c7114ba",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Finding the Antiderivative of a Radical Function"
          },
          {
